{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Leaven.</b> That which causes fermentation, and it is the known thing. Afterward he said כל אוכל מחמצת — anything that would ferment. Know that מיום הראשון עד יום השביעי is not attached to what is near it, namely ונכרתה, but rather to אוכל מחמצת, like למלוך שלמה על ישראל (1 Kings 6:1). Yefet said that there is a sign that draws itself forward and another after it backward, like מי אדם פטדה וברקת (below 25:17), whose sense is אדם ופטדה וברקת, and thus מיום הראשון עד יום השביעי:" "He already mentioned that any Israelite who eats leaven is liable to karet, and here he added the ger, who is a ger tzedek:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The verse citation למלוך שלמה על ישראל appears to match 1 Kings 5:1 in the Hebrew verse numbering (Eng. 5:32), but Ibn Ezra cites it as מ\"א ו א', i.e. 1 Kings 6:1; rendered as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:40.709107661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}